Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: prefer RI MAC on marked Nokia GDMs

The stock bootloader may supply a mac-address property independently of
the Linux ethernet aliases. On opt-in Nokia GDMs use the RI NVMEM cell
instead, so a saved ethaddr cannot replace the configured LAN and PON
addresses. A missing or invalid RI MAC is an error, not a reason to use
the bootloader address or a random one.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -4543,7 +4543,17 @@ static int airoha_alloc_gdm_device(struc
 	if (err)
 		return err;
 
-	err = of_get_ethdev_address(np, netdev);
+	if (of_property_read_bool(np, "airoha,mac-from-nvmem")) {
+		u8 addr[ETH_ALEN];
+
+		err = of_get_mac_address_nvmem(np, addr);
+		if (err)
+			return err;
+
+		eth_hw_addr_set(netdev, addr);
+	} else {
+		err = of_get_ethdev_address(np, netdev);
+	}
 	if (err) {
 		if (err == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 			return err;
